@startuml
title Connection Registration State Machine
[*] --> VERIFYING : supported registration request
VERIFYING --> STORING : identity/connectivity/permissions valid
VERIFYING --> REJECTED : parse/auth/verification fails
STORING --> READY : credential stored + Connection insert committed
STORING --> REJECTED : store/insert fails; cleanup own attempt
READY --> READY : rename + version CAS
READY --> RECHECKING : explicit verify/replace, expected version
RECHECKING --> READY : read-only verify + CAS succeeds, version + 1
RECHECKING --> READY : verify/CAS fails; prior committed record unchanged
READY --> [*]
REJECTED --> [*]
note right of READY
READY is the last successful verification, not live health.
Recheck failure is visible separately; retain committed record.
Version CAS guards edits and credential replacement.
VERIFYING/STORING/REJECTED describe request stages.
Registration does not change Organization default.
READY records a verification, not live health.
end note
note right of REJECTED
No resource provisioning during registration.
Cleanup failures are observable operational errors.
end note
@enduml
